{
  "abstract": "A Mathlib-only Lean formalization of Liu and Meng's separation argument. There exists an infinite binary sequence on which every total computable adaptive betting strategy with uniformly computable-real, nonnegative, fair capital has bounded capital, while the sequence fails a Martin-Löf test for the fair-coin measure. Each strategy queries distinct positions along every possible answer history. Martin-Löf randomness also implies randomness for this strategy convention, so the inclusion is proper. The actual simultaneous affine-block construction, short reconstruction programs, and probability estimates are proved without construction premises.",
